-- title:
--   A density floor bounds the selected and maximal-remainder product
-- statement:
--   Let $g_0$ be a maximum-cardinality edge of a hypergraph bundle $B$. Suppose $0\le a\le1$ and every base edge of cardinality $|g_0|$ has density at least $a$. Then $a^{|B.\mathrm{edges}|}$ is at most the density of the projected selected edge times the maximal-remainder main product.
